{"title":"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given a finite sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/5/595f49ae5d398ac1a14cd13844b8a508bdfa9eaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=(a_1,a_2,\\ldots ,a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> real numbers, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/496761119df26cc13f4b05a2e99254eff491d695.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(S)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> be the sequence \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/2/4325f16692282dfef51a4fe932b8a7e7d06f6a94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{a_1+a_2}{2},\\frac{a_2+a_3}{2},\\ldots ,\\frac{a_{n-1}+a_n}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"272\" height=\"43\" />\nof <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> real numbers. Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/2/0629e1540d0f6b6832668f7a21899205a274fd65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A^1(S)=A(S)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"19\" /> and, for each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d609764da0dea9c1ef12e2a493a59f90af03b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\le m\\le n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"14\" />, define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/d/86d50b8b0e9ca347e49131a9199f60b44b0132d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A^m(S)=A(A^{m-1}(S))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"19\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e28efa00c4f2c66d1aa381c0cb1f8e0ef8d6e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/8/e7889d3d5dfbbbe1d4b67b5c7563dfb7a7a85f6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=(1,x,x^2,\\ldots ,x^{100})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"19\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/c/3dcb723ecbfe28a363cc7ed75830807bffb0986b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A^{100}(S)=(1/2^{50})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"19\" />, then what is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/e/64e35d4a55651b87cedef1994b9d9750a41c3c7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } 1-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } \\sqrt{2}-1\\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } \\frac{1}{2}\\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } 2-\\sqrt{2}\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ }  \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"507\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/1/8614efa469574473ea38eae7b192f0144fe9a703.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A^1(S)=\\left(\\frac{1+x}{2},\\frac{x+x^2}{2},...,\\frac{x^{99}+x^{100}}{2}\\right)\\]\" width=\"315\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b2fdff313f1b6438eda71cb4253fba50b5ea9cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A^2(S)=\\left(\\frac{1+2x+x^2}{2^2},\\frac{x+2x^2+x^3}{2^2},...,\\frac{x^{98}+2x^{99}+x^{100}}{2^2}\\right)\\]\" width=\"469\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e00a877ac56692fbcb156eab6cdea47340edd594.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Rightarrow A^2(S)=\\left(\\frac{(x+1)^2}{2^2},\\frac{x(x+1)^2}{2^2},...,\\frac{x^{98}(x+1)^2}{2^2}\\right)\\]\" width=\"392\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>In general, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/5144ebd6a0420c6c12e1de1f1724951faafd812e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A^n(S)=\\left(\\frac{(x+1)^n}{2^n},\\frac{x(x+1)^n}{2^n},...,\\frac{x^{100-n}(x+1)^n}{2^n}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"402\" height=\"43\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/0/6a06abae962f696022be6f80d9f857a627c53126.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A^n(s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/f/fdfe87522486e4e67c34523af8e6302d6c25e1d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101-n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> terms. Specifically, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86f9dd2ca2f2f2f90a4f1906f53a67c258b961c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A^{100}(S)=\\frac{(x+1)^{100}}{2^{100}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"164\" height=\"39\" /> To find x, we need only solve the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaafc2a9f0d5f76cdfa07357c305a20e1fa2ab81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(x+1)^{100}}{2^{100}}=\\frac{1}{2^{50}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"130\" height=\"39\" />. Algebra yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abf6a55c8cf6cbe65c3fbe265f40ffcc27a61374.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\sqrt{2}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For every sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/f/13f87a6b464b02f48d0e359f4b78fe3c0f2c0270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\left(a_1,a_2,\\dots, a_n\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"20\" /> of at least three terms,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/b/48ba075ca0197cf64a8a049e454bc4002c79271b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A^2(S)=\\left(\\frac{a_1+2a_2+a_3}{4},\\frac{a_2+2a_3+a_4}{4},\\dots,\\frac{a_{n-2}+2a_{n-1}+a_n}{4}\\right).\\]\" width=\"517\" height=\"43\" />Thus for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/6/5e669db8ac7954113fb74f90b3c1f2e5959f56a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 1\\text{ and }2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"14\" />, the coefficients of the terms in the numerator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/9/4c9309ac60d0317faff7c2f426fb6ea29fbb458e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A^m(S)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"20\" /> are the binomial coefficients <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8ad1fc2bcd6a9b559049cfa355770c3798ddd938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{m}{0},\\binom{m}{1},\\dots,\\binom{m}{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"183\" height=\"55\" />, and the denominator is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f2949376cf9667bec6117d164f65945d8a2c049f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcba6e9967c8963eba73fcd8c2b088995b49f3a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{m}{r}+\\binom{m}{r+1}=\\binom{m+1}{r+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"236\" height=\"55\" /> for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39ad7957a2fccdb01077981b253b51d278609565.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />, the coefficients of the terms in the numerators of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dcae89ccd67064fc5d2e31901bb2508ee149d27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A^{m+1}(S)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"21\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/d/1ad85d225a7b9f8ad7c89fc0ffbb17bbd9945c9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{m+1}{0},\\binom{m+1}{1},\\ldots,\\binom{m+1}{m+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"277\" height=\"55\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89414b67be33dd8c8602b05eceb8480348d128.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\leq m\\leq n-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"118\" height=\"16\" />. The definition implies that the denominator of each term in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dcae89ccd67064fc5d2e31901bb2508ee149d27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A^{m+1}(S)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"21\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9e942790378476e4ea1c95e170bacf8e074fe3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{m+1}$\" width=\"36\" height=\"15\" />. For the given sequence, the sole term in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e256ea84cf5f48ff2cc1c6b94ade81b69c3b8dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A^{100}(S)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"62\" height=\"21\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/9/229c10c23d24d38577f29bc4bb8e63f9d7f33daf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2^{100}} \\sum_{m=0}^{100} \\binom{100}{m}a_{m+1} = \\frac{1}{2^{100}} \\sum_{m=0}^{100} \\binom{100}{m}x^m = \\frac{1}{2^{100}}(x+1)^{100}.\\]\" width=\"470\" height=\"53\" />Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff18c32037305d4a9f4322d5f301958ff69f62b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{1}{2^{50}}\\right)=A^{100}(S)=\\left(\\frac{(1+x)^{100}}{2^{100}}\\right),\\]\" width=\"272\" height=\"43\" />so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b49f5810b072ea5c81450459c4a43dba7927cc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+x)^{100}=2^{50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"21\" />, and because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e28efa00c4f2c66d1aa381c0cb1f8e0ef8d6e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/0/21024abae37fad5f9213a4cf797b5fe95365baee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\boxed{\\sqrt{2}-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"103\" height=\"32\" />.\n- Alcumus\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A\">2006 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a h